# Explicit pass-through for crawler-facing static files. Netlify is
# documented to serve a real file over a matching redirect rule
# automatically, but the /:username wildcard below is a literal path
# pattern that could otherwise match "robots.txt"/"sitemap.xml" as a
# username -- these explicit, more-specific rules are placed first so
# there is no ambiguity: the real static file always wins the redirect
# evaluation itself, not just the file-vs-redirect fallback. (No
# sitemap.xml exists in this repo yet; the rule is a no-op reservation
# for if/when one is added, not a claim one exists today.)
/robots.txt   /robots.txt   200
/sitemap.xml  /sitemap.xml  200

# Preserve pretty-URL access to the real app and collector app.
# Placed before the username wildcard below so it always wins.
/app        /app.html         200
/dashboard  /app.html         200
/collector  /collector.html   200

# Clean public portfolio links: tracstudio.app/username rewrites (not
# redirects, the URL bar stays clean) to the existing ?view=portfolio&
# username= query-string flow app.html already knows how to load.
# Netlify matches real files (schema.sql, assets/*, app.html, etc.) before
# ever checking redirect rules, so this wildcard only fires for paths that
# aren't an actual file, i.e. real usernames.
/:username  /app.html?view=portfolio&username=:username   200
